A utilitiy to help faultfind a Diverecorder network.  Essentally a UDP monitor recording the packets sent by DiveRecorder on four UDP ports.   The utility can also decode the packets received, assuming they from diverecorder, and also has a simple scoreboard showing some of the received data.  The monitor has a very simple metrics window which looks at the UPDATE and REFEREE packets and reports the number received.  The utility assumes that DR sends 3 packets per message which is the case for all Diverecorder versions in the last few years.  Older versions of DR may send more than 3 in which case the metrics data will be wrong.  The visulisation on the main screen has a pie chart that expects a max of 12, thus easy to visulise the number of messages received in a run as it shows as a clock face!  

The UDPSend is something I used to try and test the metrics capability of the Monitor programme.  These are not real DiveRecorder packets though.  
